# Jev + Flagship

A dependency-free TypeScript source library for semantic feature-flag evaluation in Cloudflare Workers.

Jev interprets fuzzy application attributes and chooses the best matching semantic rule. Flagship remains the control layer that handles enabled state, defaults, rule order, rollout, and the final classical JSON variation.

## How it works

```text
Application attributes
      ↓
Fetch complete Flagship definition
      ↓
Match each jev:<name> condition with state.<name>
      ↓
Jev selects one rule or default
      ↓
Selected conditions become Flagship context
      ↓
Native Flagship binding performs final evaluation
```

The library never returns a variation merely because Jev selected it. Jev chooses a semantic rule; Flagship makes the final decision.

## Add it to a Worker

Copy [`src/jev-flagship.ts`](./src/jev-flagship.ts) into your Worker project. It has no package dependencies.

Create an evaluator from your Worker bindings:

```ts
import { createJevFlagEvaluator } from './jev-flagship';
import { parseExperience } from './experience';

const evaluator = createJevFlagEvaluator({
  accountId: env.CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID,
  appId: env.FLAGSHIP_APP_ID,
  apiToken: env.FLAGSHIP_API_TOKEN,
  runJev: (input) => env.AI.run('typesafe/jev', input),
  evaluateFlag: (key, fallback, context) =>
    env.FLAGS.getObjectDetails(key, fallback, context),
});

const state = {
  match: applicationState,
};

const result = await evaluator.evaluate(
  'jev-choice-user-experience',
  state,
  parseExperience,
);
```

